 "format": "citerift-stage04-freeze/2",
 "label": "Stage 04 freeze candidate manifest (corrective cycle, D-071). Frozen scientific code: the freeze-content commit that holds this file; named with its tree and CI run by the attestation commit that follows it. Not a freeze until the owner accepts it.",
 "limitations": [
  "D-071 recall cost: a citation whose only identifier is given by the checked sources as both the original and a notice (13,681 DOIs and 1,053 PMIDs in one record, 56 DOIs and 27 PMIDs across records, in the pinned snapshot) is UNRESOLVED_IDENTITY (IDENTIFIER_ROLE_COLLISION), never positive, even when the work is truly retracted.",
  "D-072 strict resolution by a second identifier (SPEC 7.3a): a role collision is resolved only by another cited identifier that has no notice role itself, directly identifies the same work, and whose record states a different notice identifier in its scheme. Recall cost, a limitation and never a performance result: on the pinned snapshot 1,472 of 31,506 dt-1 positive DOI+PMID pairs become UNRESOLVED_IDENTITY (the declined lenient alternative would lose 800). Any future evaluation (P2) states this limitation. If the resolving identifier is itself wrong in the citation, the attachment rests on it.",
  "D-073 (reviewer finding C-01): collision is read per key over every record, so a second record of the same work (same original DOI and PMID, e.g. an expression of concern whose notice identifiers equal the article's) makes a clean retraction abstain (53 snapshot pairs, one campaign claim, ar-3351802 un-00059); no same-work-sibling exemption; 'probable true positive' is descriptive only.",
  "D-075 (corrective-cycle reviewer finding B-03 of REVIEW_B.md, the mirror of D-058): an original DOI cited with the same record's notice PMID stays positive when the DOI is clean (628 of 31,279 snapshot pairs; 30,482 are IDENTITY_CONFLICT under both tables because the record states the work's own, different PMID); the notice PMID is never positive support, and a role-collided, unavailable or absent DOI never reaches D-14 through it.",
  "The 80 campaign articles and the 232 development revisions are development evidence; the regression on them is not an evaluation and is never counted as unseen data.",
  "D-061 performance: the warm p95 of a retained investigation is above the 5 s target (NOT_MET); see the performance section of FREEZE_REPORT.md for the residual cases and bottlenecks.",
  "D-062 verification scope (D-064, owner decision OD-S12-1): each process runs the D-062 identity-verification profile (verify_index_identity: format and policy, integrity and structure, digests recomputed against the metadata, build manifest, full derivation recompute); Stage 02's per-event JSON-Schema pass runs only in Stage 02's complete verify (the certification, run in the Step 12 evidence); in the differential tamper evidence no case is rejected by that pass alone.",
  "F-11: a descendant that leaves the session by double fork or setsid is attributed and killed only while it is found in the scan; the bound is per attempt, not per investigation.",
  "The external checkpoint (D-052) detects divergence from a recorded state; it is not authentication or a signature.",
  "Investigation Memory requires a local POSIX filesystem (rename, fsync, O_NOFOLLOW, flock semantics).",
  "Evaluation labels of a future gate are AI-generated (Stage 03 precedent); not human ground truth.",
  "The Stage 02 snapshot covers Retraction Watch records up to its build; later events are not covered.",
  "Some dt-1 classes were not seen in real development data; they are covered by the Step 4 enumerated domain and synthetic tests only.",
  "A11-5: the lifecycle distinction BLOCKED versus RUNNING-and-waiting is kept in the journal and the JSON output; the user-facing status is blocked (exit 8) for both.",
  "A11-6: journals keep the absolute bundle, index and memory-root paths of the creating host as provenance; they enter no scientific digest, and moved inputs are named with --index and --bundle (no journal rewriting).",
  "The Step 4 reference model was written by the same engineering process as the production code; its independence is procedural (separate model, oracle and tests), not organisational.",
  "A-07: D-7 drops taint reasons that D-6 keeps (frozen Step 4 model and SPEC 7.3 agree).",
  "Step 12 B-03 residual: a retry whose earlier ACQUIRE side channel was deleted by someone is not detected.",
  "B-13: LOOKUP memory is bounded per query; the aggregate is queries x per-query bound.",
  "C-12: Stage 02 crossref_sources has no ORDER BY (upstream; 0 rows in the accepted RW-only index).",
  "Step 12 E-05, E-06, E-08: denominator and sensitivity-variant choices are Step 13 pre-registration decisions."
 ],
